# SpecLoom Implementation Workflow

## User entry

- **specloom-work-creator** — planning
- **specloom-implement** — implementation

Never `@` internal agents directly.

## Session contract (all 4 orchestrators)

Load **specloom-orchestrator-session**:

1. Work discovery → `no_work` → reply immediately, **no git**
2. **specloom-git** `task_start` (new branch off `ai-workflow`)
3. Work on branch
4. **specloom-git** `task_push` + `merge_to_ai_workflow` before user reply

**Priority:** specs before features. Blocked → no work.

## Pipeline

```
specloom-implement
  → specloom-worker (×10) → dev agents + specloom-worker-validation
  → specloom-validator → specloom-standardized-loop (×3) → domain validators
  → specloom-tester → specloom-test-loop (×5) → test-standards agents
  → specloom-update-knowledgebase
```

## Confidence thresholds

| Gate | Pass |
|------|------|
| Worker validation | ≥99 + app_runs |
| Validator | ≥99 |
| Tester | 100% coverage |

## Git

**specloom-git** at start + end of every orchestrator session. Base branch **`ai-workflow`**. Delegated sub-agents share parent branch.

## Legacy agents (until full migration)

Help routing still uses `sdd-system-advisor` until `specloom-advisor` lands.
